.TH IDLESCREEN 1 "October 2026" "idlescreen 4.1.10" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
idlescreen \- IdleScreen standalone screensaver and idle management suite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B idlescreen
[\fISUBCOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B idlescreen-daemon
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBidlescreen\fR is a unified idle management and screensaver suite for Linux Wayland sessions.
It features a zero-CPU event-driven daemon, built-in dynamic ASCII screensaver, and an optional
library of mathematical screensavers via \fBidlescreen-extras\fR.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B daemon
Start the IdleScreen background daemon.
.TP
.B status
Query daemon state, active inhibitors, and current display status.
.TP
.B preview [\fISAVER\fR]
Preview a screensaver effect immediately in fullscreen or terminal TUI.
.TP
.B list
List all available screensavers (built-in and installed extras).
.TP
.B set \fISAVER\fR
Set the default screensaver in configuration.
.TP
.B stop
Deactivate the currently running screensaver.
.TP
.B inhibit [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Inhibit screensaver activation while a task executes.
.TP
.B doctor [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
Perform system diagnostics and Wayland checks. Supports \fB\-\-verbose\fR and \fB\-\-json\fR.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is stored in \fB~/.config/idlescreen/config.toml\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd (1)
